	"description": [
		"This course explores algorithms for solving geometric problems. Topics include triangulations of polygons, convex hulls, Voronoi diagrams, polyhedra, shortest paths, and configuration spaces. This course can count as either the D or M perspective for the math major, and as an elective for the computer science major. Some prior experience in proof-based mathematics or computer programming is recommended."
